  "memories": [
    "KastDocument is the root of a K'UHUL Abstract Syntax Tree. It carries protocol 'kast/1', a registry hash, source kind/id, an entry node id, a list of KastNodes, a list of KastEdges, and a computed SemanticHash.",
    "KastNode preserves semantic identity across frontend projections. Each node has an Id, Kind (one of 12 enumerations: Document, Fold, Operation, Value, Tensor, Memory, Agent, Model, File, Event, Decision, Projection), a Fold, Lane, Glyph, and Opcode field for resolved semantic coordinates.",
    "KastEdge represents explicit graph relationships. Control transitions are expressed as edges rather than hidden in source syntax. Each edge has From/To node ids, Kind (Flow/Data/Call/Reference/Dependency/Association), a Label, and an Ordinal.",
    "KAST describes semantic structure without scheduling work, executing backends, performing network I/O, or bypassing XCFE admission. It is a structural bridge, not an execution engine.",
    "The canonical bridge is: frontend projection -> KAST -> XCFE -> K'UHUL pi -> SCXQ2.",
    "KastNodeKind enum: Document(0), Fold(1), Operation(2), Value(3), Tensor(4), Memory(5), Agent(6), Model(7), File(8), Event(9), Decision(10), Projection(11).",
    "KastEdgeKind enum: Flow(0), Data(1), Call(2), Reference(3), Dependency(4), Association(5).",
    "KastValueKind enum for operands: Literal(0), Symbol(1), Hash(2), Path(3)."
  ],
